            },
            {
                "comment": "Best professor in ME department. His personality and teaching style is the best!",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Prof. Dan Negrut is the type of professor you want in all of your classes. Super funny guy, brings a lot of vitality to the zoom lectures. This class is one of my favorite classes at UW-Madison. The weekly programming assignments are a lot of work, but they are definitely doable.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "The HWs are a lot of work, and require a lot of self-teaching outside of class. However, the material isn't overly difficult. Grading is fair, and exams are reasonable - challenging, but not impossible.",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Awesome professor that makes your learn and work for your grade",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Great teacher! He's good at presenting the material and giving you exposure to the ideas and technologies behind HPC. He's more focused on you learning than making the class impossible. The class is a lot of work but not hard to do well in if you put in the work. Great class!",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Seems to be someone who really cares about the students. The material he presents is well made and is very good to get acquainted with High performance computing with CUDA, OpenMP and so on.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Lenient grader",
                "difficulty_rating": 1,
